# The kernel creates /dev/dma_heap/* with mode 0600 root:root.  This rule was
# added for ARM's GBM: it allocated the session's window/scanout buffers from a
# dma-buf heap, so without it gbm_create_device() failed, wlroots logged "Failed
# to create GBM device" and quietly fell back to the CPU renderer (pixman).
#
# That path is retired -- the GPU runs panfrost, which allocates through GEM and
# does not need a heap (docs/FINDINGS.md section 20.7).  The rule stays because
# opening the heaps is not specific to Mali and costs nothing here, but nothing
# in this image depends on it any more.
SUBSYSTEM=="dma_heap", MODE="0666"
